1
00:00:09,698 --> 00:00:10,598
(All names of people, places,
and entities are fictional.)

2
00:00:10,598 --> 00:00:11,598
(The filming of minors and animals
complied with the guidelines.)

3
00:00:11,598 --> 00:00:12,565
(Generative AI technology was used
in some scenes.)

4
00:00:14,232 --> 00:00:15,732
One rainy spring day,

5
00:00:16,098 --> 00:00:17,532
we met on the street.

6
00:00:18,665 --> 00:00:20,765
It was just my grandmother and me...

7
00:00:21,032 --> 00:00:23,965
until a little ball of fur came along
and became part of our family.

8
00:00:24,532 --> 00:00:27,632
I'm afraid she won't live much longer.

9
00:00:28,498 --> 00:00:31,265
At first, the cat was very sick.

10
00:00:32,332 --> 00:00:35,598
I wanted to spend
even one more day with her,

11
00:00:35,598 --> 00:00:37,765
so I named her Haru.

12
00:00:38,565 --> 00:00:40,032
As if she understood how I felt,

13
00:00:40,032 --> 00:00:43,465
Haru miraculously grew healthier
with each passing day.

14
00:00:43,898 --> 00:00:46,198
As my clumsy playing turned into music...

15
00:00:46,198 --> 00:00:48,165
and as I grew up,

16
00:00:48,698 --> 00:00:51,698
Haru was always
part of every melody I played.

17
00:00:53,165 --> 00:00:55,232
It was Haru who helped me...

18
00:00:55,232 --> 00:00:58,298
get back on my feet
after I lost my grandmother.

19
00:01:00,432 --> 00:01:04,198
And Haru passed away.

20
00:01:07,198 --> 00:01:09,732
(A Letter for You)

21
00:01:10,698 --> 00:01:12,265
And from that day on,

22
00:01:12,265 --> 00:01:13,232
Na Eun.

23
00:01:13,932 --> 00:01:14,732
Na Eun.

24
00:01:15,698 --> 00:01:18,198
I couldn't bring myself
to step onstage again.

25
00:01:22,432 --> 00:01:23,465
Why aren't you singing?

26
00:01:24,365 --> 00:01:25,498
Stop it.

27
00:01:25,798 --> 00:01:28,498
I'm sorry.

28
00:01:42,065 --> 00:01:43,032
<i>Your</i>

29
00:02:19,864 --> 00:02:25,097
<i>Between the lingering notes</i>

30
00:02:25,365 --> 00:02:26,732
Haru, how is it? Do you like it?

31
00:02:36,032 --> 00:02:37,932
(Na Eun and Haru)

32
00:02:48,232 --> 00:02:49,932
I'm giving you this
since you asked me for this,

33
00:02:50,998 --> 00:02:52,607
but are you really going
to sell your instrument too?

34
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,965
I'm done with music.

35
00:02:54,965 --> 00:02:58,065
Don't you think
you're being a little dramatic?

36
00:02:58,832 --> 00:03:01,065
It's not like this is the first audition
you've failed.

37
00:03:01,065 --> 00:03:02,498
Why would you say that here?

38
00:03:02,498 --> 00:03:04,932
Every time, you'd write another song
and get right back onstage.

39
00:03:04,932 --> 00:03:07,698
Now you're talking about stage fright
and giving up music...

40
00:03:07,698 --> 00:03:09,198
just because your cat died...

41
00:03:11,032 --> 00:03:11,865
Na Eun,

42
00:03:13,298 --> 00:03:14,832
you can still come by anytime.

43
00:03:15,798 --> 00:03:17,065
You don't have to sing.

44
00:03:41,665 --> 00:03:43,932
(Choi Seung Hun)

45
00:03:46,732 --> 00:03:47,898
Na Eun,

46
00:03:47,898 --> 00:03:49,065
why are you ignoring my messages?

47
00:03:49,432 --> 00:03:50,832
I've got nothing to say.

48
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,065
- Bye.
- Are you really done with music?

49
00:03:58,198 --> 00:03:59,265
Seung Hun, please.

50
00:03:59,265 --> 00:04:00,065
Na Eun?

51
00:04:00,465 --> 00:04:02,132
This is the animal hospital.

52
00:04:02,132 --> 00:04:03,965
Oh, hi.

53
00:04:04,498 --> 00:04:06,265
We found Haru's collar.

54
00:04:10,732 --> 00:04:13,032
- Ma'am!
- Hi, Na Eun.

55
00:04:13,898 --> 00:04:14,965
Did you run all the way here?

56
00:04:14,965 --> 00:04:16,398
You didn't have to rush.

57
00:04:16,398 --> 00:04:17,432
Where's the collar?

58
00:04:17,432 --> 00:04:18,665
Oh, right.

59
00:04:19,465 --> 00:04:20,265
Here.

60
00:04:21,932 --> 00:04:25,898
That's an animal language translator,
isn't it?

61
00:04:26,732 --> 00:04:27,598
A translator?

62
00:04:27,598 --> 00:04:29,365
There's no screen,

63
00:04:29,932 --> 00:04:32,665
so I think you have to use an app
to check it.

64
00:04:32,665 --> 00:04:34,632
It's still powered on too.

65
00:04:35,465 --> 00:04:38,132
There might be
some recordings saved on it.

66
00:04:41,265 --> 00:04:44,165
I had no idea. I thought
it was just an ordinary collar.

67
00:04:46,865 --> 00:04:50,632
Could Haru's last words be saved...

68
00:04:51,198 --> 00:04:52,398
on this?

69
00:04:55,198 --> 00:04:56,065
Oh, it's on.

70
00:04:56,698 --> 00:04:59,732
"Access has been restricted
due to prolonged inactivity."

71
00:04:59,732 --> 00:05:01,765
"Please visit a retailer."

72
00:05:01,765 --> 00:05:02,598
A retailer?

73
00:05:04,198 --> 00:05:06,998
It was a gift, so I don't know
where it came from.

74
00:05:07,865 --> 00:05:09,565
By the way, where did you find it?

75
00:05:09,565 --> 00:05:11,665
We searched everywhere back then,
but we couldn't find it.

76
00:05:11,665 --> 00:05:12,532
Well,

77
00:05:13,865 --> 00:05:15,465
yesterday...

78
00:05:15,465 --> 00:05:16,798
So it...

79
00:05:17,432 --> 00:05:18,332
Delivery!

80
00:05:19,165 --> 00:05:20,865
Where should I leave these?

81
00:05:22,065 --> 00:05:23,465
Oh, that collar!

82
00:05:26,865 --> 00:05:28,265
Was it yesterday?

83
00:05:28,265 --> 00:05:29,598
Yes, I'm sure it was.

84
00:05:30,465 --> 00:05:34,698
The moment I opened the door
to drop off a package yesterday,

85
00:05:34,698 --> 00:05:36,765
all the dogs and cats...

86
00:05:40,065 --> 00:05:40,965
started barking and meowing at once.

87
00:05:41,298 --> 00:05:46,065
And they were all gathered
under that bench over there.

88
00:05:46,065 --> 00:05:49,898
They kept looking at the bench,
then at me, over and over again.

89
00:05:49,898 --> 00:05:52,965
So I wondered
if there was something underneath.

90
00:05:52,965 --> 00:05:55,898
I bent down to take a look.

91
00:05:55,898 --> 00:05:56,832
And guess what?

92
00:05:56,832 --> 00:05:58,865
There was a light flashing underneath!

93
00:05:58,865 --> 00:06:02,065
Something was blinking
way back in that dark space!

94
00:06:05,465 --> 00:06:08,098
That's right. He was the one who found it.

95
00:06:09,932 --> 00:06:13,632
By the way, you've got
some incredible rhythm!

96
00:06:14,632 --> 00:06:17,832
You noticed that already!

97
00:06:18,565 --> 00:06:19,532
That's right.

98
00:06:19,532 --> 00:06:22,098
I used to be in a military band.

99
00:06:22,398 --> 00:06:23,598
<i>Neither look up nor look down</i>

100
00:06:23,598 --> 00:06:25,065
<i>Turn</i>

101
00:06:25,065 --> 00:06:26,165
And check under the bench.

102
00:06:26,832 --> 00:06:27,932
I was the band's vocalist.

103
00:06:29,132 --> 00:06:31,032
Thank you so much.

104
00:06:32,165 --> 00:06:35,732
By the way, do you happen to know
where I can buy one of these?

105
00:06:35,732 --> 00:06:37,332
Of course, I do!

106
00:06:37,765 --> 00:06:38,698
A delivery driver, remember?

107
00:06:38,698 --> 00:06:41,498
That's an animal language translator.

108
00:06:42,532 --> 00:06:46,165
I saw them
at the little variety store over there.

109
00:06:46,165 --> 00:06:47,098
A variety store?

110
00:07:04,532 --> 00:07:05,498
Excuse me!

111
00:07:17,932 --> 00:07:19,132
Hello?

112
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:24,565
Excuse me!

113
00:07:25,198 --> 00:07:26,065
Maybe no one is here.

114
00:07:26,065 --> 00:07:27,065
Hello?

115
00:07:28,565 --> 00:07:30,098
- You found the place pretty quickly.
- You scared me!

116
00:07:30,098 --> 00:07:31,965
You scared me even more.

117
00:07:33,365 --> 00:07:34,198
Hi.

118
00:07:35,065 --> 00:07:36,565
The owner should be inside.

119
00:07:37,298 --> 00:07:39,832
Hello!

120
00:07:40,298 --> 00:07:41,132
What?

121
00:07:41,798 --> 00:07:42,732
Oh, my gosh.

122
00:07:42,732 --> 00:07:43,965
What's all the commotion?

123
00:07:44,732 --> 00:07:47,032
This girl came here about the translator.

124
00:07:48,098 --> 00:07:49,665
Where should I put these?

125
00:07:50,398 --> 00:07:52,965
Does that translator even work?

126
00:07:56,098 --> 00:07:56,998
A translator?

127
00:07:57,632 --> 00:07:59,265
I just want to check the messages on it.

128
00:08:08,165 --> 00:08:08,998
This thing won't work.

129
00:08:09,932 --> 00:08:12,032
It's a really old model,
and it's discontinued.

130
00:08:12,032 --> 00:08:13,198
They don't even offer support anymore.

131
00:08:13,198 --> 00:08:14,865
Then what about Haru's messages?

132
00:08:14,865 --> 00:08:17,032
It clearly said I should visit a retailer.

133
00:08:17,332 --> 00:08:19,498
I don't know. We just sell them here.

134
00:08:19,498 --> 00:08:21,065
Then where's the manufacturer?

135
00:08:21,665 --> 00:08:23,365
- How would I know?
- Someone from the company, maybe?

136
00:08:23,365 --> 00:08:25,332
I told you, I don't know!

137
00:08:25,332 --> 00:08:27,065
Ma'am, help me, please.

138
00:08:27,065 --> 00:08:28,665
I'll pay whatever it takes.

139
00:08:28,665 --> 00:08:31,032
I have to know what Haru said.

140
00:08:32,132 --> 00:08:33,532
Let go of me!

141
00:08:33,532 --> 00:08:36,198
I told you I can't help you! Good grief!

142
00:08:36,198 --> 00:08:38,898
Please! I'll do anything you ask me to!

143
00:08:38,898 --> 00:08:41,165
What do you mean,
you'll do anything I ask?

144
00:08:41,165 --> 00:08:44,332
Just let go of me!

145
00:08:45,998 --> 00:08:46,765
Wait a minute!

146
00:08:51,132 --> 00:08:52,965
Isn't that a guitar pick?

147
00:08:54,465 --> 00:08:55,332
Yes, it is.

148
00:08:56,265 --> 00:08:57,065
Guitar pick?

149
00:08:58,298 --> 00:08:59,132
Are you a musician?

150
00:09:00,632 --> 00:09:01,765
I was.

151
00:09:03,432 --> 00:09:04,698
What do you mean, you were?

152
00:09:07,832 --> 00:09:10,598
You want me to audition?

153
00:09:13,198 --> 00:09:13,998
Gosh.

154
00:09:14,532 --> 00:09:15,598
Don't get any ideas!

155
00:09:16,065 --> 00:09:17,498
I'm the one auditioning!

156
00:09:18,098 --> 00:09:21,098
I just want you to write a song for me.

157
00:09:21,432 --> 00:09:22,265
Look,

158
00:09:22,965 --> 00:09:25,765
it says original songs earn extra points.

159
00:09:27,365 --> 00:09:29,698
You're entering the audition?

160
00:09:30,365 --> 00:09:31,432
So what?

161
00:09:32,132 --> 00:09:33,498
What's wrong with me entering an audition?

162
00:09:36,265 --> 00:09:38,332
It's been on my bucket list forever.

163
00:09:39,998 --> 00:09:41,432
I can play guitar too.

164
00:09:41,932 --> 00:09:43,575
I picked up a few things
by watching other people play.

165
00:09:45,365 --> 00:09:49,365
But I quit music.

166
00:09:51,165 --> 00:09:53,198
Didn't you say you'd do anything I asked?

167
00:09:53,532 --> 00:09:54,665
Anything but music.

168
00:09:54,665 --> 00:09:55,865
I'll do anything else.

169
00:09:56,765 --> 00:09:59,998
The deadline to apply is
coming up pretty soon.

170
00:10:00,364 --> 00:10:02,824
Then you can just write it
again this time.

171
00:10:03,190 --> 00:10:05,776
You wanted to hear
what your cat had to say, didn't you?

172
00:10:06,163 --> 00:10:08,330
I want to audition too.

173
00:10:08,603 --> 00:10:10,375
Don't you know you have
to give something to get something?

174
00:10:27,578 --> 00:10:29,584
- That jerk.
- Ma'am?

175
00:10:29,771 --> 00:10:30,744
Oh, my gosh.

176
00:10:38,777 --> 00:10:40,603
That's him, right?

177
00:10:40,651 --> 00:10:42,317
Yes, that's him.

178
00:10:42,611 --> 00:10:44,877
That creepy music again.

179
00:10:44,924 --> 00:10:48,103
We really need to catch that guy!

180
00:10:48,197 --> 00:10:51,311
You know I have
another part-time job in the evenings.

181
00:10:51,697 --> 00:10:53,863
I have to get going now.

182
00:10:53,891 --> 00:10:56,931
Then what am I supposed to do on my own?

183
00:10:58,091 --> 00:10:59,150
Well...

184
00:11:03,847 --> 00:11:04,680
Me?

185
00:11:24,014 --> 00:11:25,954
What's that man doing?

186
00:11:26,354 --> 00:11:28,240
I'm telling you,
I've seen him several times.

187
00:11:28,284 --> 00:11:31,564
He's been putting something strange
in the cats' food. Go catch him!

188
00:11:31,638 --> 00:11:33,524
Me? All by myself?

189
00:11:33,564 --> 00:11:35,544
I'm too scared.

190
00:11:35,604 --> 00:11:39,030
He's a big, intimidating guy
dressed all in black.

191
00:11:39,058 --> 00:11:42,530
He's this tall.

192
00:11:43,151 --> 00:11:44,257
And he's ridiculously fast.

193
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:46,070
Whenever I get even a little close,

194
00:11:46,070 --> 00:11:48,483
he freaks out and runs off
in the blink of an eye.

195
00:11:49,164 --> 00:11:53,741
And you expect me to catch
someone that big, scary, and fast...

196
00:11:54,361 --> 00:11:55,416
all by myself?

197
00:12:04,068 --> 00:12:07,987
Oh, look at that creep!
He's putting something in the cats' food!

198
00:12:08,041 --> 00:12:10,208
Hurry! You have to go now!

199
00:12:12,241 --> 00:12:13,314
Excuse me!

200
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:17,194
Did you just put something in that food?

201
00:12:17,888 --> 00:12:18,541
Oh...

202
00:12:22,141 --> 00:12:23,081
Hello.

203
00:12:24,341 --> 00:12:25,041
"Hello?"

204
00:12:25,128 --> 00:12:26,554
Don't give me that "hello" nonsense!

205
00:12:26,668 --> 00:12:28,514
Where do you think you're going?

206
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:31,981
- I'm sorry!
- What are you sorry for?

207
00:12:32,008 --> 00:12:34,114
Why did you put something
in the cats' food?

208
00:12:34,154 --> 00:12:37,274
- The cats were meowing so much.
- How much could they...

209
00:12:37,314 --> 00:12:38,754
possibly have been meowing?

210
00:12:38,779 --> 00:12:40,741
- I'm sorry!
- Did she really have to go that far?

211
00:12:40,766 --> 00:12:42,355
They were meowing so much,
I thought they might be sick,

212
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:44,536
- so I added some supplements...
- As if!

213
00:12:44,561 --> 00:12:47,314
I'm serious! They're just supplements!

214
00:12:48,947 --> 00:12:49,927
Supplements?

215
00:12:55,236 --> 00:12:56,636
They're just supplements...

216
00:12:58,669 --> 00:12:59,623
Please be gentle.

217
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:05,274
- That hurts.
- I'm sorry.

218
00:13:05,299 --> 00:13:07,893
- Easy, please.
- Okay.

219
00:13:09,667 --> 00:13:11,847
Why did you run away?

220
00:13:13,366 --> 00:13:16,379
Well, some people don't like it
when you feed stray cats.

221
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:21,766
And when you came toward me earlier,
you really scared me.

222
00:13:23,346 --> 00:13:24,360
I'm sorry.

223
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:27,700
It's okay.

224
00:13:28,233 --> 00:13:29,740
I probably would've gotten
the wrong idea too.

225
00:13:29,807 --> 00:13:34,200
Still, you can't just go
around kicking people like that.

226
00:13:34,353 --> 00:13:35,053
Right?

227
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:36,753
Especially someone you've never met.

228
00:13:37,287 --> 00:13:41,853
If you work here,
you must know a lot about cameras.

229
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:47,280
What's a good camera for getting
those really stylish shots these days?

230
00:13:47,313 --> 00:13:49,720
Most cameras take
really sharp pictures these days.

231
00:13:50,447 --> 00:13:51,787
But if you want something with character,

232
00:13:56,498 --> 00:13:57,278
I'd recommend this one.

233
00:13:58,464 --> 00:14:00,262
The focus isn't great.

234
00:14:00,287 --> 00:14:02,295
It lets in too much light,
and the image quality isn't the best.

235
00:14:02,498 --> 00:14:04,625
But the footage actually looks
pretty amazing.

236
00:14:05,331 --> 00:14:06,265
How should I put it?

237
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:10,411
It's almost like it's telling you
that it's okay to be a little imperfect.

238
00:14:12,841 --> 00:14:16,401
Someday, I'd really love to shoot
something properly with this.

239
00:14:17,362 --> 00:14:18,462
My own movie.

240
00:14:19,195 --> 00:14:21,241
My dream is to become a film director.

241
00:14:21,528 --> 00:14:23,308
Okay! You're in!

242
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,075
I'm in?

243
00:14:25,215 --> 00:14:29,361
Oh, I'm entering a singing competition.

244
00:14:29,888 --> 00:14:32,801
I want you to film my audition video.

245
00:14:32,988 --> 00:14:34,201
Wait, why are you doing this?

246
00:14:34,241 --> 00:14:35,588
What did he ever do to you?

247
00:14:35,635 --> 00:14:38,008
What's the problem?
He says he wants to be a film director.

248
00:14:38,122 --> 00:14:41,922
Having a director shoot my video
gives me a head start!

249
00:14:43,973 --> 00:14:45,073
"A director?"

250
00:14:45,993 --> 00:14:48,193
Then could I shoot
a music video for you too?

251
00:14:48,546 --> 00:14:49,772
A music video too?

252
00:14:49,813 --> 00:14:52,799
I could just shoot a few extra scenes
while we're filming your audition.

253
00:14:53,459 --> 00:14:55,812
I've always wanted to try making one.

254
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:58,619
Okay! Sounds good!

255
00:14:59,233 --> 00:15:02,859
Now it's all up to you, Na Eun.

256
00:15:27,735 --> 00:15:29,014
Haven't you been writing any songs lately?

257
00:15:33,395 --> 00:15:34,642
What are you doing here?

258
00:15:34,742 --> 00:15:36,789
Why? I can smoke here now, can't I?

259
00:15:36,975 --> 00:15:38,055
The cat's gone.

260
00:15:38,983 --> 00:15:39,997
I knew it.

261
00:15:40,029 --> 00:15:41,822
You really need me to take care of you.

262
00:15:42,382 --> 00:15:44,842
Your music and everything else are
a complete mess when I leave you alone.

263
00:15:47,536 --> 00:15:49,810
What are you doing
in someone else's house?

264
00:15:52,590 --> 00:15:53,203
Someone else's?

265
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:58,076
Why are you so touchy?

266
00:15:58,790 --> 00:15:59,496
Huh?

267
00:16:02,356 --> 00:16:05,276
Don't tell me you're still acting
like this over that stupid cat.

268
00:16:05,490 --> 00:16:06,763
That stupid cat?

269
00:16:08,450 --> 00:16:10,803
Haru was the one who stayed
by my side all this time.

270
00:16:10,915 --> 00:16:14,302
Not you, who got wasted and disappeared
on the day my grandma died.

271
00:16:14,403 --> 00:16:17,163
Darn it. That stupid cat again.

272
00:16:18,336 --> 00:16:21,262
Hey. How long are you going
to keep going on about that cat?

273
00:16:22,223 --> 00:16:25,370
I'm offering to live with you,
so just say yes already.

274
00:16:25,463 --> 00:16:27,156
Please, just leave.

275
00:16:28,816 --> 00:16:30,342
What are you going to do without me?

276
00:16:34,222 --> 00:16:35,168
Fine, I'm leaving.

277
00:16:36,348 --> 00:16:37,787
And get rid of this stuff already.

278
00:17:02,673 --> 00:17:04,823
(Used instrument pickup tomorrow.
Leave them outside for pickup.)

279
00:17:21,852 --> 00:17:22,946
What's all this?

280
00:17:26,896 --> 00:17:28,222
I'll write you a song.

281
00:17:30,289 --> 00:17:30,942
Really?

282
00:17:31,694 --> 00:17:35,507
But you have to promise
to fix the translator.

283
00:17:58,728 --> 00:18:00,074
Is this where we work?

284
00:18:00,421 --> 00:18:02,274
Yes. Why?

285
00:18:02,728 --> 00:18:04,708
It's not bad, is it?

286
00:18:08,348 --> 00:18:11,621
But when are we going
to clean all this up?

287
00:18:11,648 --> 00:18:12,421
Right now.

288
00:18:12,568 --> 00:18:13,501
Right now?

289
00:18:15,975 --> 00:18:16,908
Hello!

290
00:18:17,755 --> 00:18:18,528
Hi!

291
00:18:19,122 --> 00:18:20,862
Why are you here so early?

292
00:18:20,942 --> 00:18:23,468
We're not supposed
to shoot the video until later.

293
00:18:23,575 --> 00:18:24,875
I called him.

294
00:18:25,335 --> 00:18:27,628
It'll take the two of us forever
to clean all this up.

295
00:18:29,568 --> 00:18:30,788
Where should I start?

296
00:18:31,762 --> 00:18:34,768
All right, shall we start cleaning?

297
00:18:35,435 --> 00:18:36,722
Here, take this.

298
00:18:36,902 --> 00:18:39,361
Na Eun, put your instruments over there.

299
00:18:39,415 --> 00:18:40,755
Okay, this way.

300
00:18:50,819 --> 00:18:52,686
We should clear everything out
over here too, right?

301
00:18:52,731 --> 00:18:53,458
Yes!

302
00:18:55,872 --> 00:18:58,192
I'll move the bed over there!

303
00:18:58,217 --> 00:18:59,015
Okay!

304
00:18:59,621 --> 00:19:01,325
Ma'am, what's this?

305
00:19:01,326 --> 00:19:03,245
What are you doing? Don't touch it.

306
00:19:03,465 --> 00:19:04,816
Hey, follow me.

307
00:19:04,985 --> 00:19:06,785
Come on.

308
00:19:08,412 --> 00:19:09,588
Careful.

309
00:19:09,652 --> 00:19:11,957
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

310
00:19:12,205 --> 00:19:13,992
I've had a feeling since the first time...

311
00:19:14,226 --> 00:19:16,629
that you're a girl who needs
a lot of taking care of.

312
00:19:17,325 --> 00:19:18,430
I'm sorry.

313
00:19:36,715 --> 00:19:37,783
Testing.

314
00:19:40,066 --> 00:19:41,586
Put on a song.

315
00:19:41,887 --> 00:19:43,077
Let's check the speaker.

316
00:19:53,362 --> 00:19:55,767
Why are you playing such a sad song?

317
00:20:01,573 --> 00:20:03,108
I've been listening to this a lot lately.

318
00:20:03,489 --> 00:20:04,142
Huh?

319
00:20:04,376 --> 00:20:05,811
It must've turned on automatically.

320
00:20:06,478 --> 00:20:07,846
Why do you keep listening to that song?

321
00:20:09,581 --> 00:20:11,316
It feels like
how I've been feeling lately.

322
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:15,053
Haru died in the spring too.

323
00:20:19,871 --> 00:20:21,506
I guess I'll check your song.

324
00:20:21,507 --> 00:20:22,327
Can I?

325
00:20:27,599 --> 00:20:29,019
"Our Days?"

326
00:20:29,132 --> 00:20:30,068
What's this song?

327
00:20:30,236 --> 00:20:31,636
You can't listen to this one.

328
00:20:32,977 --> 00:20:34,172
Why not?

329
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:35,907
Because...

330
00:20:37,279 --> 00:20:39,111
I made it with Haru.

331
00:20:41,046 --> 00:20:43,486
You made a song with a cat?

332
00:20:43,939 --> 00:20:45,784
Haru was my muse.

333
00:20:46,418 --> 00:20:47,786
Whenever I played music,

334
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:49,855
Haru loved it more than anyone.

335
00:20:49,877 --> 00:20:50,922
A muse?

336
00:20:51,823 --> 00:20:53,125
A cat was your muse?

337
00:20:56,328 --> 00:20:57,863
Oh, sorry.

338
00:21:05,637 --> 00:21:07,372
Why did you stop writing this song?

339
00:21:08,006 --> 00:21:09,107
It doesn't even have a title.

340
00:21:11,366 --> 00:21:13,311
I couldn't write anymore
after Haru was gone.

341
00:21:15,073 --> 00:21:18,650
Have you completely lost your drive?

342
00:21:20,499 --> 00:21:21,553
Are you getting any sleep?

343
00:21:23,674 --> 00:21:24,456
Are you eating?

344
00:21:26,758 --> 00:21:29,461
How are you supposed to do anything
when you're so frail?

345
00:21:29,954 --> 00:21:32,597
You won't be able to write my song either.

346
00:21:33,665 --> 00:21:34,800
This is a real problem.

347
00:21:38,969 --> 00:21:39,838
Wait a minute.

348
00:21:42,841 --> 00:21:44,843
Let's see.

349
00:21:45,101 --> 00:21:48,046
I definitely saw it
while rummaging through the boxes.

350
00:21:48,094 --> 00:21:50,029
Here it is.

351
00:21:50,054 --> 00:21:51,676
(Marine Corps)

352
00:21:59,341 --> 00:22:01,760
Why did the boss tell us to wear this?

353
00:22:02,828 --> 00:22:03,662
I know, right?

354
00:22:14,646 --> 00:22:16,174
From now on,

355
00:22:16,786 --> 00:22:19,377
we're starting intensive training
for the audition.

356
00:22:21,146 --> 00:22:22,314
Remember,

357
00:22:22,359 --> 00:22:25,884
your physical stamina is directly tied
to my chances of passing.

358
00:22:27,919 --> 00:22:29,646
But what about the shop?

359
00:22:33,792 --> 00:22:34,593
Welcome.

360
00:22:34,893 --> 00:22:36,094
How may I help you?

361
00:22:37,963 --> 00:22:39,163
I left it in a friend's hands.

362
00:22:39,493 --> 00:22:41,266
All right, let's go.

363
00:22:44,564 --> 00:22:45,737
There you go!

364
00:22:47,091 --> 00:22:48,673
You too. Get going.

365
00:22:49,307 --> 00:22:50,584
Why me?

366
00:22:56,381 --> 00:22:57,983
Na Eun, wait for me!

367
00:22:58,009 --> 00:22:58,650
Oh, no.

368
00:23:00,085 --> 00:23:01,049
Na Eun.

369
00:23:01,050 --> 00:23:04,156
One, two. That's it.

370
00:23:07,083 --> 00:23:07,993
You must be hungry.

371
00:23:09,510 --> 00:23:10,228
Sorry?

372
00:23:19,806 --> 00:23:20,672
All right.

373
00:23:22,006 --> 00:23:23,241
Ta-da.

374
00:23:26,211 --> 00:23:28,046
Did you make this yourself?

375
00:23:29,207 --> 00:23:30,315
My lunchbox.

376
00:23:31,213 --> 00:23:32,250
Where's my lunchbox?

377
00:23:32,547 --> 00:23:33,151
Oh, no.

378
00:23:34,319 --> 00:23:37,189
Well, just eat for now.

379
00:23:37,656 --> 00:23:39,324
You need to eat well to write good songs.

380
00:23:40,536 --> 00:23:41,893
Here we go.

381
00:23:42,227 --> 00:23:43,461
Hocus pocus.

382
00:23:43,462 --> 00:23:44,696
What are you sprinkling?

383
00:23:44,776 --> 00:23:46,031
Magic powder.

384
00:23:46,451 --> 00:23:48,600
Probiotics. It's good for your health.

385
00:23:49,178 --> 00:23:50,001
Here.

386
00:23:51,911 --> 00:23:52,504
Open up.

387
00:23:55,818 --> 00:23:56,608
I said open up.

388
00:24:06,918 --> 00:24:08,753
How long do we have to keep doing this?

389
00:24:09,754 --> 00:24:10,689
Haven't you slept?

390
00:24:10,774 --> 00:24:13,441
I told you to get some sleep.

391
00:24:13,925 --> 00:24:15,493
At least close your eyes.

392
00:24:22,167 --> 00:24:25,136
The night air feels nice.

393
00:24:26,471 --> 00:24:28,471
The sound of crickets is even better.

394
00:24:31,163 --> 00:24:33,111
It's like a lullaby.

395
00:24:35,205 --> 00:24:35,946
Listen.

396
00:25:34,335 --> 00:25:35,540
Can I name the song?

397
00:25:38,008 --> 00:25:39,210
Sure. Go ahead.

398
00:25:39,644 --> 00:25:41,413
"On a Summer Night." How about that?

399
00:25:44,182 --> 00:25:45,350
"On a Summer Night?"

400
00:25:46,384 --> 00:25:47,319
I like it.

401
00:25:48,992 --> 00:25:50,154
What do you think, Director?

402
00:25:51,732 --> 00:25:52,724
Pretty.

403
00:25:53,132 --> 00:25:53,792
What?

404
00:25:55,026 --> 00:25:55,760
Huh?

405
00:25:57,100 --> 00:25:57,862
I mean,

406
00:25:58,797 --> 00:26:00,699
the title is pretty.

407
00:26:12,210 --> 00:26:15,146
I'll work on the lyrics tonight,

408
00:26:15,413 --> 00:26:18,286
and then start recording tomorrow...

409
00:26:18,287 --> 00:26:19,818
You scared me.

410
00:26:20,485 --> 00:26:22,754
Change that alarm sound already.

411
00:26:24,689 --> 00:26:25,724
Sorry,

412
00:26:26,363 --> 00:26:28,793
but it's time to clean up the cat bowls.

413
00:26:30,029 --> 00:26:31,996
You even clean up the cat bowls?

414
00:26:34,760 --> 00:26:35,616
Go with her.

415
00:26:35,749 --> 00:26:36,468
You two.

416
00:26:36,649 --> 00:26:37,569
Get some fresh air too.

417
00:26:38,169 --> 00:26:40,096
You beat him up pretty badly.

418
00:26:40,572 --> 00:26:42,039
So help him out as much as you can.

419
00:26:42,816 --> 00:26:44,542
I have to close up the shop.

420
00:26:44,569 --> 00:26:45,610
You two, hurry up.

421
00:26:45,809 --> 00:26:46,569
I'm tired.

422
00:26:46,683 --> 00:26:47,203
Bye.

423
00:26:57,255 --> 00:26:58,189
Shall we go?

424
00:26:59,023 --> 00:26:59,591
Yes.

425
00:27:04,142 --> 00:27:06,698
Did you set an alarm
just to clean up here?

426
00:27:07,888 --> 00:27:10,435
I made a promise
to the neighborhood representative.

427
00:27:10,835 --> 00:27:13,371
I feed the cats but keep the area clean.

428
00:27:14,708 --> 00:27:16,708
How long have you been feeding cats?

429
00:27:17,708 --> 00:27:19,708
For about 15 years.

430
00:27:23,314 --> 00:27:24,482
When I was little,

431
00:27:25,250 --> 00:27:27,552
I once brought home a sick kitten
from the street.

432
00:27:28,586 --> 00:27:30,388
I secretly took care of it in my room,

433
00:27:30,835 --> 00:27:32,023
but while I was at school,

434
00:27:33,258 --> 00:27:35,258
my mom threw it back out on the street.

435
00:27:36,628 --> 00:27:37,862
That's when it started.

436
00:27:39,124 --> 00:27:40,665
I thought the kitten might eat it.

437
00:27:46,344 --> 00:27:48,273
It must've taken a lot
for that kitten to trust me.

438
00:27:50,757 --> 00:27:52,877
It must've felt abandoned all over again.

439
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:01,853
No matter how late I got home,

440
00:28:02,454 --> 00:28:05,957
Grandma and Haru would get up,
all sleepy and disheveled, to greet me.

441
00:28:06,891 --> 00:28:09,494
That alone was enough to make
all my exhaustion disappear.

442
00:28:11,129 --> 00:28:13,364
I still live on that memory.

443
00:28:15,669 --> 00:28:16,701
So I'm sure...

444
00:28:17,335 --> 00:28:19,771
that cat remembers too.

445
00:28:20,678 --> 00:28:23,007
It remembers how much you cared for it.

446
00:28:24,976 --> 00:28:27,312
And I'm sure it was happy.

447
00:28:37,689 --> 00:28:39,691
I'll get going now.

448
00:28:40,191 --> 00:28:41,159
See you tomorrow.

449
00:29:05,690 --> 00:29:08,525
(I will pass the audition!)

450
00:29:14,974 --> 00:29:16,308
(Na Eun and Haru)

451
00:29:36,777 --> 00:29:37,744
Couldn't sleep again?

452
00:29:39,213 --> 00:29:40,413
I just couldn't fall asleep.

453
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:42,682
I was at a cafe sorting tracks to record.

454
00:29:43,117 --> 00:29:45,551
Why at a cafe when you have a home?

455
00:29:49,990 --> 00:29:51,157
You don't want to be home.

456
00:29:51,725 --> 00:29:53,759
You do this every single night.

457
00:29:54,595 --> 00:29:56,829
We have to do something about this.

458
00:29:56,830 --> 00:29:58,231
I couldn't sleep either.

459
00:29:59,366 --> 00:30:00,299
Why not?

460
00:30:02,369 --> 00:30:04,970
I was nervous about the shoot.

461
00:30:09,142 --> 00:30:11,176
Then should we start
with the instruments today?

462
00:30:12,045 --> 00:30:12,845
Sounds good.

463
00:30:13,281 --> 00:30:14,413
Let's go.

464
00:31:02,329 --> 00:31:05,031
I think backing vocals should
come in here.

465
00:31:05,699 --> 00:31:06,766
You do it, Na Eun.

466
00:31:07,868 --> 00:31:09,035
Me?

467
00:31:09,770 --> 00:31:10,903
I can't.

468
00:31:10,904 --> 00:31:12,037
Oh, come on.

469
00:31:12,038 --> 00:31:14,206
It's just a little backing vocal.

470
00:31:14,207 --> 00:31:16,108
Come on, Na Eun.

471
00:31:16,310 --> 00:31:20,580
It's just for a second. All you do is hum.

472
00:31:20,814 --> 00:31:21,881
You're doing it, okay?

473
00:31:23,017 --> 00:31:25,284
Come on, just this once.

474
00:31:25,586 --> 00:31:26,986
Hello!

475
00:31:27,287 --> 00:31:29,255
Where could you be?

476
00:31:29,389 --> 00:31:32,458
Hello. Oh, there you are.

477
00:31:32,894 --> 00:31:34,160
I looked all over for you.

478
00:31:34,528 --> 00:31:37,296
I've got a fresh delivery for you.

479
00:31:38,999 --> 00:31:40,199
Oh, the army band!

480
00:31:48,775 --> 00:31:49,908
Well, look at this.

481
00:31:49,909 --> 00:31:52,778
("On a Summer Night")

482
00:32:05,159 --> 00:32:08,560
Now that I'm about to sing,
I'm so nervous.

483
00:32:10,231 --> 00:32:11,530
And there's a camera.

484
00:32:12,866 --> 00:32:15,668
Don't mind the camera.
I'll make you look great.

485
00:32:16,404 --> 00:32:18,738
Just relax. We can always record it again.

486
00:32:19,006 --> 00:32:20,839
Let's go have fun when we're done.

487
00:32:21,609 --> 00:32:22,775
Oh, I'd love that.

488
00:32:25,345 --> 00:32:26,679
We'll start now.

489
00:32:45,966 --> 00:32:49,335
<i>On a breeze</i>

490
00:32:49,336 --> 00:32:52,505
<i>That's still so warm</i>

491
00:32:52,873 --> 00:32:59,578
<i>The evening glow slowly spreads</i>

492
00:32:59,579 --> 00:33:06,184
<i>For no reason at all</i>

493
00:33:06,185 --> 00:33:11,623
<i>Thoughts of me begin to bloom</i>

494
00:33:13,427 --> 00:33:18,965
<i>On this summer night</i>

495
00:33:19,833 --> 00:33:26,005
<i>Like a breeze that softly blows</i>

496
00:33:27,140 --> 00:33:33,412
<i>You tickle and stir my heart</i>

497
00:33:34,014 --> 00:33:40,453
<i>Like a midsummer dream</i>

498
00:33:40,887 --> 00:33:46,458
- <i>In your eyes</i>
- <i>In your eyes</i>

499
00:33:47,294 --> 00:33:53,665
- <i>Shining stars fill up the sky</i>
- <i>Shining stars fill up the sky</i>

500
00:33:54,568 --> 00:34:00,973
- <i>Even in this lingering moment</i>
- <i>Even in this lingering moment</i>

501
00:34:01,441 --> 00:34:06,945
- <i>Think of my name</i>
- <i>Think of my name</i>

502
00:34:07,448 --> 00:34:11,752
- <i>Ah-ha, ah-ha, ah-ha</i>
- <i>Ah-ha, ah-ha, ah-ha</i>

503
00:34:11,753 --> 00:34:14,954
- <i>Ah</i>
- <i>Ah</i>

504
00:34:14,955 --> 00:34:19,926
- <i>Ah-ha, ah-ha, ah-ha</i>
- <i>Ah-ha, ah-ha, ah-ha</i>

505
00:34:33,173 --> 00:34:36,408
You look so happy
when you make music, Na Eun.

506
00:34:39,180 --> 00:34:40,646
I'm not quite happy with it.

507
00:34:42,382 --> 00:34:44,383
The backing vocals stick out.

508
00:34:45,085 --> 00:34:46,518
- The backing vocals?
- Yes.

509
00:34:47,921 --> 00:34:51,557
It needs a woman's voice
to really come alive.

510
00:34:52,860 --> 00:34:54,927
Why don't you do it, Na Eun?

511
00:34:57,131 --> 00:34:59,331
I want to hear you sing too.

512
00:35:10,143 --> 00:35:11,210
Right?

513
00:35:11,211 --> 00:35:12,144
(You have two new messages.)

514
00:35:12,145 --> 00:35:16,281
(Choi Seung Hun)

515
00:35:26,326 --> 00:35:28,160
Isn't this the song you wrote, Na Eun?

516
00:35:28,929 --> 00:35:31,497
Hold on, that's our song.

517
00:35:32,265 --> 00:35:34,099
What about my audition?

518
00:35:34,100 --> 00:35:36,168
<i>The evening glow slowly spreads</i>

519
00:35:37,504 --> 00:35:39,105
I'm sorry. I should get going.

520
00:35:39,940 --> 00:35:40,872
What?

521
00:35:43,043 --> 00:35:44,043
Na Eun.

522
00:36:04,334 --> 00:36:06,101
Did you hear it? Well?

523
00:36:06,837 --> 00:36:07,837
It sounds much better, right?

524
00:36:08,306 --> 00:36:10,439
Take it down now. It's my song.

525
00:36:10,440 --> 00:36:12,373
I stayed up all night busting my butt...

526
00:36:12,374 --> 00:36:14,276
on that piece of junk.

527
00:36:14,978 --> 00:36:15,878
So how is it yours?

528
00:36:15,879 --> 00:36:17,780
I'm not letting it go this time.

529
00:36:18,982 --> 00:36:20,816
Yeah? Go ahead and try.

530
00:36:26,757 --> 00:36:29,892
Who are people going to believe?
A hit producer...

531
00:36:30,828 --> 00:36:33,729
or someone who can't even get on a stage?

532
00:36:34,531 --> 00:36:36,832
So stop being so stubborn...

533
00:36:37,968 --> 00:36:38,968
and start over with me.

534
00:36:39,769 --> 00:36:41,637
I could look over your songs like before.

535
00:36:42,205 --> 00:36:44,773
- Let go.
- Who would listen to your songs but me?

536
00:36:44,774 --> 00:36:46,909
- Let go!
- You thief!

537
00:36:49,346 --> 00:36:50,313
Let go of her hand.

538
00:36:50,816 --> 00:36:51,914
Is it you?

539
00:36:52,249 --> 00:36:54,683
Get over here. Why, you little!

540
00:36:54,684 --> 00:36:56,951
Calm down.
Let's talk when you've cooled off.

541
00:36:56,952 --> 00:36:58,454
I'm not angry.

542
00:36:58,455 --> 00:37:01,290
- Let go of me.
- You're obviously angry.

543
00:37:01,625 --> 00:37:03,659
And you! Let go of her hand now.

544
00:37:06,096 --> 00:37:08,130
Hey, get over here right now.

545
00:37:08,365 --> 00:37:09,598
Who are you?

546
00:37:11,902 --> 00:37:13,069
Hey!

547
00:37:15,038 --> 00:37:15,904
And you.

548
00:37:16,473 --> 00:37:17,339
You're really talented.

549
00:37:18,542 --> 00:37:19,476
Your music...

550
00:37:20,778 --> 00:37:21,711
is really good.

551
00:37:23,415 --> 00:37:24,780
It hits me right here.

552
00:37:26,917 --> 00:37:30,453
Don't ever let
what this jerk says scare you.

553
00:37:32,522 --> 00:37:33,522
Am I wrong?

554
00:37:35,159 --> 00:37:36,626
Why are you just standing there?

555
00:37:39,062 --> 00:37:40,562
You say something too.

556
00:37:42,166 --> 00:37:43,199
You're beautiful.

557
00:37:48,338 --> 00:37:50,205
I mean,

558
00:37:51,174 --> 00:37:52,741
everything about you is beautiful.

559
00:37:54,644 --> 00:37:56,211
More than my camera can capture.

560
00:37:57,247 --> 00:38:00,215
You looked beautiful even when you kicked
someone to protect the cats.

561
00:38:00,994 --> 00:38:02,760
You look beautiful when you make music.

562
00:38:03,294 --> 00:38:05,694
Everything about you is beautiful.

563
00:38:09,794 --> 00:38:10,694
But I guess...

564
00:38:12,694 --> 00:38:15,694
you couldn't see what was
right in front of you.

565
00:38:16,627 --> 00:38:17,460
What?

566
00:38:17,544 --> 00:38:18,378
At least for me,

567
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:21,460
when the person I like shines,

568
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:23,794
I don't block that light.

569
00:38:25,027 --> 00:38:27,594
So you should move now.

570
00:38:29,294 --> 00:38:30,427
I approve.

571
00:38:31,453 --> 00:38:34,253
What have you been doing out there?

572
00:38:34,660 --> 00:38:36,027
And who are these people?

573
00:38:36,494 --> 00:38:38,794
I'm Kim Na Eun's fan. So what?

574
00:38:38,878 --> 00:38:40,811
Didn't you hear him telling you to move?

575
00:38:41,094 --> 00:38:41,927
Go away!

576
00:38:44,960 --> 00:38:45,794
Forget it.

577
00:38:46,394 --> 00:38:47,427
We'll talk next time.

578
00:38:47,427 --> 00:38:48,627
What? Why you...

579
00:38:48,894 --> 00:38:49,860
What next time?

580
00:38:50,594 --> 00:38:51,760
Don't you dare come back!

581
00:38:57,127 --> 00:38:58,094
If he comes back,

582
00:38:59,327 --> 00:39:00,160
call me.

583
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:01,960
Okay?

584
00:39:06,160 --> 00:39:07,260
This won't do.

585
00:39:10,527 --> 00:39:12,060
I'm worried that he'll come back.

586
00:39:13,360 --> 00:39:14,360
Let me sleep over.

587
00:39:23,060 --> 00:39:23,927
You can't sleep?

588
00:39:24,927 --> 00:39:26,460
What about the audition?

589
00:39:26,794 --> 00:39:28,827
You said it was on your bucket list.

590
00:39:28,827 --> 00:39:29,794
I'm sorry I kept you from auditioning.

591
00:39:29,794 --> 00:39:31,127
How is it your fault?

592
00:39:31,127 --> 00:39:32,794
It's because of that thief!

593
00:39:32,794 --> 00:39:35,060
It was such a big opportunity!

594
00:39:35,960 --> 00:39:37,127
This is so frustrating.

595
00:39:44,994 --> 00:39:46,294
Are you okay, Na Eun?

596
00:39:47,894 --> 00:39:48,827
I...

597
00:39:50,794 --> 00:39:51,727
just...

598
00:39:55,594 --> 00:39:57,660
really miss Haru.

599
00:40:08,727 --> 00:40:10,360
("A Letter for You")

600
00:40:11,127 --> 00:40:12,860
"A Letter for You."

601
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:16,160
You said you only listen to this, right?

602
00:40:17,460 --> 00:40:19,494
("A Letter for You")

603
00:40:30,527 --> 00:40:32,994
I guess I'll do my audition here.

604
00:40:39,494 --> 00:40:42,594
Please go easy on me, Judge.

605
00:41:06,327 --> 00:41:09,694
<i>When I call your name</i>

606
00:41:13,260 --> 00:41:16,460
<i>You turn and hold me close</i>

607
00:41:20,360 --> 00:41:23,394
<i>Your warm, familiar scent</i>

608
00:41:23,394 --> 00:41:25,660
<i>More than any scent of spring</i>

609
00:41:26,594 --> 00:41:30,827
<i>Lingers long after you're gone</i>

610
00:41:33,527 --> 00:41:39,594
<i>I still miss you</i>

611
00:41:40,427 --> 00:41:46,260
<i>You're still deep within my heart</i>

612
00:41:48,594 --> 00:41:54,494
<i>Whenever I pass the places
we used to walk together</i>

613
00:41:54,494 --> 00:41:59,627
<i>I find myself looking down</i>

614
00:42:08,294 --> 00:42:09,627
Look at you.

615
00:42:20,160 --> 00:42:25,960
<i>When we meet again</i>

616
00:42:26,560 --> 00:42:32,394
<i>I'll be the first to run to you</i>

617
00:42:34,827 --> 00:42:37,527
<i>All I couldn't put into words</i>

618
00:42:37,927 --> 00:42:40,694
<i>I'll give you my whole heart</i>

619
00:42:40,694 --> 00:42:45,594
<i>And love you even more</i>

620
00:42:47,094 --> 00:42:51,727
<i>Love you</i>

621
00:43:06,227 --> 00:43:08,394
You have to send spring off quickly...

622
00:43:08,394 --> 00:43:09,727
for summer to come.

623
00:43:10,794 --> 00:43:12,627
You'll get sick
if you keep holding on to it.

624
00:43:13,560 --> 00:43:18,827
I'm sure Haru wouldn't want you
to keep holding on to spring either.

625
00:43:20,327 --> 00:43:21,560
See the summer...

626
00:43:21,860 --> 00:43:25,994
and live well
through all the seasons to come.

627
00:43:26,660 --> 00:43:28,827
That way, when you meet again,

628
00:43:29,560 --> 00:43:31,660
you'll have a lot to tell Haru.

629
00:43:32,927 --> 00:43:33,694
Right?

630
00:44:25,660 --> 00:44:26,727
Welcome.

631
00:44:27,427 --> 00:44:28,860
Ma'am!

632
00:44:30,494 --> 00:44:31,494
I have a favor to ask you.

633
00:44:32,260 --> 00:44:33,160
What is it?

634
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:39,660
<i>The window by the sunlight</i>

635
00:44:39,660 --> 00:44:42,194
<i>The warmth remained</i>

636
00:44:42,194 --> 00:44:43,060
It's really good, right?

637
00:44:44,494 --> 00:44:46,527
Yes, it's good,

638
00:44:48,727 --> 00:44:50,960
but can we just post it like that?

639
00:44:53,333 --> 00:44:55,700
I've already missed my shot
at the audition.

640
00:44:56,301 --> 00:44:59,334
I might feel better
if I at least post this.

641
00:45:01,027 --> 00:45:03,427
What if Na Eun gets angry?

642
00:45:04,860 --> 00:45:07,094
Don't worry. I'll take all the blame.

643
00:45:07,794 --> 00:45:08,560
Okay.

644
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:15,227
You can't just work
as a kitchen assistant.

645
00:45:16,194 --> 00:45:18,260
You only ever did music your whole life.

646
00:45:20,194 --> 00:45:20,960
Na Eun.

647
00:45:21,794 --> 00:45:24,160
Working in the kitchen is harder
than it looks.

648
00:45:25,827 --> 00:45:26,994
I have to do something.

649
00:45:29,660 --> 00:45:30,694
Sorry, excuse me.

650
00:45:33,927 --> 00:45:34,994
Hello?

651
00:45:34,994 --> 00:45:37,194
Hello, I'm calling from KS Label.

652
00:45:37,494 --> 00:45:38,827
Am I speaking to Kim Na Eun?

653
00:45:39,494 --> 00:45:40,927
You passed the online stage,

654
00:45:40,927 --> 00:45:43,327
so I called to inform you
about the in-person audition.

655
00:45:43,694 --> 00:45:45,560
But I never applied.

656
00:45:45,560 --> 00:45:47,894
You applied on the day of the deadline.

657
00:45:48,460 --> 00:45:49,994
With "Our Days," your own song.

658
00:45:50,394 --> 00:45:51,194
Sorry?

659
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:55,794
I'm sorry for uploading the video
without your permission.

660
00:45:58,694 --> 00:46:00,827
Your song was just too good.

661
00:46:01,127 --> 00:46:02,760
See? They called you right away.

662
00:46:04,260 --> 00:46:05,860
How could you do this without asking me?

663
00:46:06,576 --> 00:46:08,043
I told you I'm not singing anymore.

664
00:46:08,127 --> 00:46:11,594
Come on. Let's get you ready
for the audition.

665
00:46:11,594 --> 00:46:12,927
Warm up your voice.

666
00:46:14,794 --> 00:46:16,594
What do you know about me anyway?

667
00:46:19,894 --> 00:46:21,260
Right, I don't.

668
00:46:22,660 --> 00:46:23,794
But I can see it.

669
00:46:24,860 --> 00:46:28,727
You look so happy when you make music.

670
00:46:28,817 --> 00:46:30,450
Why would you quit?

671
00:46:30,894 --> 00:46:32,094
Just because of that cat?

672
00:46:34,560 --> 00:46:36,627
When the spotlight lands on me,

673
00:46:37,960 --> 00:46:39,760
I can't see anything around me.

674
00:46:40,427 --> 00:46:42,927
Not the audience, not the stage. Nothing.

675
00:46:44,594 --> 00:46:46,360
Then I am reminded of Haru.

676
00:46:47,860 --> 00:46:49,660
Haru, all alone in her final moments.

677
00:46:50,160 --> 00:46:51,860
You're going too far.

678
00:46:52,594 --> 00:46:54,627
You've been sad enough.

679
00:46:55,060 --> 00:46:57,594
Even that day, I went off
to an audition...

680
00:46:57,594 --> 00:46:59,460
and left Haru home alone, sick.

681
00:47:00,694 --> 00:47:03,627
Haru would have been waiting for me
as she died.

682
00:47:04,594 --> 00:47:07,027
How can I sing as if nothing happened?

683
00:47:16,627 --> 00:47:17,427
Follow me.

684
00:47:20,294 --> 00:47:22,960
(Closure Notice:
The stage is closed today too.)

685
00:47:24,294 --> 00:47:25,794
We can't go inside.

686
00:47:26,994 --> 00:47:29,394
My friend works security here at night.

687
00:47:30,794 --> 00:47:31,860
Hey friend!

688
00:47:33,060 --> 00:47:33,927
Security here.

689
00:47:34,460 --> 00:47:35,394
You're here.

690
00:47:35,394 --> 00:47:36,827
Everything's ready.

691
00:47:38,760 --> 00:47:39,527
Let's go.

692
00:47:44,527 --> 00:47:46,194
You don't have to go
to the audition tomorrow.

693
00:47:47,427 --> 00:47:49,794
But sing here just once.

694
00:47:51,027 --> 00:47:53,360
The song that you made with your cat.

695
00:47:54,727 --> 00:47:55,594
Haru?

696
00:47:56,560 --> 00:47:58,427
You said Haru liked your song.

697
00:48:00,253 --> 00:48:02,777
Imagine that you're singing it for Haru.

698
00:48:06,637 --> 00:48:07,730
I'll be outside.

699
00:48:15,486 --> 00:48:16,366
Ma'am.

700
00:48:24,796 --> 00:48:25,750
Please stay and listen.

701
00:48:27,023 --> 00:48:27,636
Okay.

702
00:49:31,066 --> 00:49:33,567
<i>The window by the sunlight</i>

703
00:49:34,042 --> 00:49:36,770
<i>The warmth remained</i>

704
00:49:37,314 --> 00:49:40,363
<i>Whenever I call your name</i>

705
00:49:40,997 --> 00:49:43,170
<i>You run into my arms</i>

706
00:49:43,712 --> 00:49:49,500
<i>Between the silent notes</i>

707
00:49:49,794 --> 00:49:53,782
<i>Your laughter lingers</i>

708
00:49:53,940 --> 00:49:58,432
<i>And tears well up in my eyes</i>

709
00:49:59,858 --> 00:50:04,919
<i>The words I love you</i>

710
00:50:06,250 --> 00:50:11,098
<i>Could never capture all this season holds</i>

711
00:50:12,602 --> 00:50:18,225
<i>I hold you in my heart every day</i>

712
00:50:18,660 --> 00:50:23,402
<i>As I go on living</i>

713
00:50:23,702 --> 00:50:27,944
<i>In the glow of our days together</i>

714
00:50:27,977 --> 00:50:31,005
<i>I'll sing with joy</i>

715
00:50:31,089 --> 00:50:37,370
<i>I'll carry each day of yours
in my heart as I go</i>

716
00:50:37,765 --> 00:50:43,674
<i>Even beneath cloudy skies</i>

717
00:50:43,699 --> 00:50:48,554
<i>Even if I stop for a moment</i>

718
00:50:49,013 --> 00:50:53,474
<i>When the breeze turns warm again</i>

719
00:50:53,499 --> 00:50:58,602
<i>Our days</i>

720
00:50:59,030 --> 00:51:02,358
<i>Will shine again</i>

721
00:51:04,944 --> 00:51:07,967
<i>Will shine again</i>

722
00:51:11,651 --> 00:51:16,016
<i>Will shine again</i>

723
00:51:34,899 --> 00:51:37,026
It's such a beautiful song.

724
00:51:38,466 --> 00:51:40,286
And your voice is even more beautiful.

725
00:51:40,799 --> 00:51:43,226
I knew you'd nail it!

726
00:51:46,575 --> 00:51:47,635
How are you feeling now?

727
00:51:52,089 --> 00:51:53,502
Like a weight's been lifted
off my shoulders.

728
00:51:58,400 --> 00:52:01,466
You're going
to the audition tomorrow, right?

729
00:52:06,387 --> 00:52:07,889
(Kim Na Eun)

730
00:52:12,280 --> 00:52:13,347
Why isn't she here yet?

731
00:52:13,567 --> 00:52:14,460
I don't know.

732
00:52:15,707 --> 00:52:16,934
Wait!

733
00:52:18,906 --> 00:52:20,959
Ma'am! Jun Young!

734
00:52:22,473 --> 00:52:24,073
Why are you so late?

735
00:52:24,740 --> 00:52:27,126
I took the song back from the thief.

736
00:52:28,433 --> 00:52:29,220
Really?

737
00:52:29,920 --> 00:52:30,660
How?

738
00:52:31,227 --> 00:52:32,333
I threatened him.

739
00:52:32,520 --> 00:52:33,400
What did you say?

740
00:52:34,458 --> 00:52:37,207
I still have the camera I set up
to see Haru.

741
00:52:37,536 --> 00:52:39,092
It recorded everything,

742
00:52:39,116 --> 00:52:41,220
from you sneaking in
to stealing my sheet music.

743
00:52:41,247 --> 00:52:44,886
And he went, "So, what?"

744
00:52:44,920 --> 00:52:47,367
So I said, "Take it down right now,"

745
00:52:47,533 --> 00:52:50,293
"or I'll go to the police."

746
00:52:50,700 --> 00:52:51,987
And he got scared.

747
00:52:52,012 --> 00:52:52,966
Hold on.

748
00:52:54,767 --> 00:52:57,027
Did you have a pet camera at home?

749
00:52:57,440 --> 00:52:58,413
I was lying.

750
00:52:59,227 --> 00:53:01,073
But it worked.

751
00:53:04,861 --> 00:53:08,387
Na Eun. Keep that confidence
and show them what you've got.

752
00:53:09,287 --> 00:53:12,047
That song deserves to be heard
by more people.

753
00:53:12,307 --> 00:53:13,767
That's so true.

754
00:53:15,727 --> 00:53:18,787
Ms. Kim Na Eun. You'll be next.

755
00:53:21,663 --> 00:53:23,650
- Don't be nervous.
- Okay.

756
00:53:24,936 --> 00:53:27,903
Ma'am, I kept my promise,

757
00:53:27,943 --> 00:53:29,783
so you should keep yours too.

758
00:53:31,209 --> 00:53:31,815
What promise?

759
00:53:31,969 --> 00:53:33,149
About the translator.

760
00:53:34,269 --> 00:53:36,502
I'll go in there and pass that audition.

761
00:53:39,564 --> 00:53:41,497
Ma'am, don't forget the translator.

762
00:53:42,651 --> 00:53:43,496
You got this!

763
00:53:48,008 --> 00:53:49,221
Thankfully, I didn't.

764
00:53:55,519 --> 00:53:56,259
I'm sorry.

765
00:53:57,472 --> 00:54:01,992
I did everything I could to fix it.

766
00:54:03,967 --> 00:54:05,221
But nothing worked.

767
00:54:08,013 --> 00:54:09,113
No way.

768
00:54:10,786 --> 00:54:11,780
I'm so sorry.

769
00:54:13,819 --> 00:54:14,813
I couldn't fix it.

770
00:54:17,886 --> 00:54:18,999
No.

771
00:54:19,813 --> 00:54:21,213
No, ma'am.

772
00:54:21,259 --> 00:54:24,853
Please don't cry.

773
00:54:25,686 --> 00:54:27,313
I feel so bad.

774
00:54:30,754 --> 00:54:33,001
Even if Haru said she hated me,

775
00:54:33,114 --> 00:54:37,327
I really want to know
what her last words were.

776
00:54:40,493 --> 00:54:43,393
Let me try again.

777
00:54:43,480 --> 00:54:44,886
Hang on.

778
00:54:56,145 --> 00:54:59,085
Suddenly, it's working!

779
00:54:59,439 --> 00:55:00,805
Really? Are you sure?

780
00:55:01,533 --> 00:55:03,289
Don't come any closer.

781
00:55:03,782 --> 00:55:04,556
What?

782
00:55:04,581 --> 00:55:07,787
Listen from over there.
It's a little cramped here.

783
00:55:08,667 --> 00:55:10,553
I'm sorry. I'm just really curious.

784
00:55:11,053 --> 00:55:12,333
I know.

785
00:55:12,860 --> 00:55:14,739
I understand how you feel.

786
00:55:14,767 --> 00:55:16,300
So take it easy.

787
00:55:16,600 --> 00:55:18,853
Stay there and listen.

788
00:55:23,506 --> 00:55:25,186
"I had a good life."

789
00:55:25,920 --> 00:55:30,472
"Fifteen years is a long life for a cat."

790
00:55:31,770 --> 00:55:34,190
"So please stop being sad."

791
00:55:34,390 --> 00:55:38,057
"And please meet a good guy..."

792
00:55:39,150 --> 00:55:42,743
"who'll feed cats."

793
00:55:43,717 --> 00:55:45,384
"Keep singing too."

794
00:55:45,870 --> 00:55:48,550
"I love your music."

795
00:55:49,097 --> 00:55:50,383
"It's heartwarming."

796
00:55:52,797 --> 00:55:57,697
"Don't be sad
looking at the scratches on your arms."

797
00:55:58,450 --> 00:56:03,197
"And stop crying when you see
the clumps of my fur under the sofa."

798
00:56:03,763 --> 00:56:05,010
"Get rid of them."

799
00:56:05,070 --> 00:56:06,424
"They're not good for you."

800
00:56:08,217 --> 00:56:11,297
"I believe in you,
no matter what anyone says."

801
00:56:11,824 --> 00:56:13,564
"Everything is going to be okay."

802
00:56:15,557 --> 00:56:16,497
"Thank you."

803
00:56:17,277 --> 00:56:23,370
"You made every day of my life
feel like spring."

804
00:56:24,430 --> 00:56:25,957
"Let's meet again."

805
00:56:26,190 --> 00:56:27,730
"I'll be waiting for you."

806
00:56:28,657 --> 00:56:29,564
"Goodbye."

807
00:56:30,937 --> 00:56:31,777
That's all.

808
00:56:35,071 --> 00:56:36,344
You're lying.

809
00:56:37,838 --> 00:56:38,544
What?

810
00:56:40,039 --> 00:56:42,579
I know there's nothing there.

811
00:56:43,652 --> 00:56:47,031
Still, thank you.

812
00:56:52,133 --> 00:56:53,907
By the way, ma'am.

813
00:56:56,109 --> 00:57:00,855
Do you think Haru really felt that way?

814
00:57:01,847 --> 00:57:02,949
Of course.

815
00:57:03,449 --> 00:57:05,449
I know a thing or two about cats.

816
00:57:06,185 --> 00:57:08,321
That little one may have been
grumpy sometimes,

817
00:57:10,022 --> 00:57:12,391
but she loved you so much.

818
00:57:13,282 --> 00:57:15,027
That's just how cats are.

819
00:57:15,728 --> 00:57:19,465
So don't ever blame yourself...

820
00:57:19,466 --> 00:57:21,633
for what happened to your cat. Okay?

821
00:57:24,570 --> 00:57:25,805
Thank you.

822
00:57:26,572 --> 00:57:27,874
Thank you so much.

823
00:57:29,462 --> 00:57:31,878
How can I ever repay you for all this?

824
00:57:32,591 --> 00:57:35,448
Repay me? I didn't do anything.

825
00:57:38,520 --> 00:57:39,880
Well, if you're...

826
00:57:40,626 --> 00:57:42,121
really that grateful,

827
00:57:44,790 --> 00:57:47,593
how about a hug?

828
00:58:04,602 --> 00:58:05,678
Take care.

829
00:58:07,613 --> 00:58:09,248
Thank you.

830
00:58:09,802 --> 00:58:10,917
I'll come visit again.

831
00:58:25,841 --> 00:58:29,361
(Purr and More)

832
00:58:41,800 --> 00:58:42,896
That lady was...

833
00:58:44,517 --> 00:58:46,118
weirdly easy to be around.

834
00:58:59,291 --> 00:59:00,533
Haru.

835
00:59:01,867 --> 00:59:02,969
Goodbye.

836
00:59:06,605 --> 00:59:07,740
Thank you for everything.

837
00:59:13,269 --> 00:59:14,981
Let's meet again someday.

838
00:59:43,175 --> 00:59:44,343
Has Na Eun left?

839
00:59:45,851 --> 00:59:46,645
Yes.

840
00:59:49,648 --> 00:59:50,683
Your bucket list was...

841
00:59:51,422 --> 00:59:53,422
all about Na Eun.

842
00:59:56,995 --> 01:00:00,933
(Haru's Bucket List: 1. Finish her song.
2. Get her away from that jerk.)

843
01:00:00,958 --> 01:00:04,974
(3. Help Na Eun find someone good.
4. Keep Na Eun healthy.)

844
01:00:04,999 --> 01:00:08,777
(5. Get Na Eun back onstage.)

845
01:00:14,147 --> 01:00:15,107
How was it?

846
01:00:18,677 --> 01:00:19,779
It's a bit of a shame.

847
01:00:23,249 --> 01:00:25,518
If you were going
to let me see her again anyway,

848
01:00:29,121 --> 01:00:31,357
you could've let me be my real self.

849
01:00:34,369 --> 01:00:35,194
I'm sorry.

850
01:00:36,181 --> 01:00:37,229
Those are the rules.

851
01:00:48,167 --> 01:00:51,210
Well, it's time to go.

852
01:00:52,578 --> 01:00:53,412
You should go...

853
01:00:54,180 --> 01:00:55,314
and join the others...

854
01:00:56,449 --> 01:00:57,583
and rest.

855
01:00:58,453 --> 01:00:59,185
Haru?

856
01:01:00,686 --> 01:01:02,288
The name Haru was...

857
01:01:03,689 --> 01:01:05,558
given to me by Na Eun...

858
01:01:06,092 --> 01:01:07,560
so I could live happily...

859
01:01:08,247 --> 01:01:11,362
every single day.

860
01:01:14,533 --> 01:01:15,167
And...

861
01:01:17,173 --> 01:01:18,337
I was happy.

862
01:01:20,459 --> 01:01:21,941
Every single day.

863
01:01:56,475 --> 01:01:57,309
It was truly...

864
01:01:58,767 --> 01:02:02,848
such a wonderful time.

865
01:02:05,047 --> 01:02:07,953
Just like the day I first met...

866
01:02:08,967 --> 01:02:09,955
Na Eun.

867
01:02:14,007 --> 01:02:19,864
(A Letter for You)

868
01:02:42,443 --> 01:02:43,322
(Marine Corps)

869
01:02:43,346 --> 01:02:46,193
(Fifteen years ago)

870
01:02:46,194 --> 01:02:47,774
Excuse me, have you seen a kitten?

871
01:02:48,766 --> 01:02:50,196
It looks like this.

872
01:02:51,263 --> 01:02:54,600
The owner of that shop over there
feeds the stray cats.

873
01:02:54,601 --> 01:02:55,801
You should go ask.

874
01:02:56,814 --> 01:02:58,938
Thank you.

875
01:03:11,890 --> 01:03:13,959
The kitten was really sick.

876
01:03:14,553 --> 01:03:15,754
Do you think it'll be okay?

877
01:03:16,298 --> 01:03:17,623
Don't worry.

878
01:03:17,765 --> 01:03:19,811
I'm sure a really good person took it.

879
01:03:19,812 --> 01:03:20,726
A pretty one too.

880
01:03:21,794 --> 01:03:22,728
Really?

881
01:03:22,905 --> 01:03:24,296
Yes, of course.

882
01:03:25,864 --> 01:03:26,865
What a relief.

883
01:03:27,763 --> 01:03:29,763
I should've at least filmed a video.

884
01:03:31,737 --> 01:03:33,272
Haru.

885
01:03:34,673 --> 01:03:36,275
Hi, Haru.

886
01:03:37,556 --> 01:03:38,944
I'm here.

887
01:03:39,896 --> 01:03:41,680
How was your day today?

888
01:03:49,847 --> 01:03:54,304
(To everyone who loves
a Haru of their own)
